
Naming the Cells
======================

Formula for having using same cell content and will not change the value of the cell:
=I6*$K$1 ---< vy putting the $ sign in front of the letter and number in cell key.

Naming the cell: this is other way to implement this: by naming the cell --> highlight the cell with the value,
go to the left side Name Box and giev the cell a name, without spaces, using dash sign

Go to Formula ribbon, use the "Use in Formula" to remmeber what you named the cell

Go to "Name Manager" to see the formula you've made 

To name cells header: select all data, go to Defined Names --> select "Create from Selection",
Choose what rows or columns: this time choose the "Top row" to select the header, click ok
Now, go to Defined Names --> select "Name Manager", fro there you will see the name of each top row cells


XLOOKUP - searches vertically or horizonatally for a lookup value
===========

In a cell type = xlookup( < click the arrow down in a formula bar beside the text view> )
"Function Arguments" window will open, fill up "Lookup_value", "Lookup_array", and "Return_array"
"Lookup_value" --> Notebook - (what we are looking up)
"Lookup_array" --> product Name - where we are going to look B6:B74
"Return_array" --> Price C6:C74

Use ctrl key + shift key + arrow down to select all what is in the column, click ok
=XLOOKUP(B1,B6:B74,C6:C74,"Not Found",,-1)



XLOOKUP DATA MINING - Look at different table
===========
Use ctrl key + shift key + arrow down to select all what is in the column, click ok
=XLOOKUP(H2,$D$2:$D$73,$E$2:$E$73)

Use F4 to automatically append the $ sign.

IF FUNCTION
==============
type =if(  click the arrow down in a formula bar beside the text view> )
Set the following in the argument fields:
- Logical_test - any value expression that can be evaluated to TRUE or FALSE
- Value_if_true
- Value_if_false
click ok
=IF(B5>=3,"Bonus","No Bonus")
=IF(F5=1,"Soup",IF(F5=2,"Sandwich","Salad"))

For nested if click inside the () of if() to show the new logic_test




DATABASE FUNCTION
==================
Category = field where you are going to put your item that you are searching

COUNTIF() - counting how many items that you are l;ooking for
=COUNTIF(C5:C62,F5)

SUMIF() - searching the items that you are looking for then adding each expenses of it.
=SUMIF(C5:C62,F5,D5:D62)

AVERAGEIF() - searching the items that you are looking for then getting the average of each expenses of it.
=AVERAGEIF(C5:C62,F5,D5:D62)


